    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0411" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg315"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mason to Mr. Uhl.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Frankfort</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 314.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instructions No. 153 of
                    May 3, and my report of May 22 in response thereto, I have now to transmit
                    herewith an officially sealed sample of evaporated apples taken from a lot which
                    was imported by Mi. Erwin Roelker, of Frankfort, from Albert Petri, of
                    Rochester, N. Y., and which have been condemned by the police and health
                    authorities of Frankfort as containing, per kilogram, from 0.0035 to 0.0515 gram
                    of zinc or salts of zinc, a proportion which is adjudged prejudicial to human
                    health.</p>
                <p>This sample bears the Real and certificate of the police court before which the
                    proceedings against Mr. J. Latscha, the retailer of the apples took place.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank H. Mason</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
